From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: tomaszstaniak <68373859+tomaszstaniak@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 16 Oct 2026 19:16:30 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] Security: enforce the automation read boundary on stored
 smart-filter params

Backport of upstream b630d7cb9aeb2a79ab5224ebf6e8266f1d858873 (#5684),
engine and test parts only.

Smart filters store a command id and params in the document, so a crafted
document could make a re-render read a file outside the automation roots
(colour-lookup LUT files) without the authorize gate: synchronous
smart-object rendering has no Session argument, job threads dropped the
requesting session's authority, and a trusted render could warm the
process-wide stack cache with a stage the gate never saw.

The requesting session's gate travels in a thread-local (jobs.rs), entered
around command execution and Session::edit and reinstalled on job workers
and job apply. render_in and apply_filter_to_surface recheck stored filter
commands before any source resolution or cache lookup; a denial is an
error, not unfiltered pixels. layer.smartFilter.setParams re-authorizes the
merged params. A denial leaves the document unchanged.

Not taken from the commit: the wasm profile change in Cargo.toml and the
ui_set description text in automation/src/server.rs (unrelated). This base
has no resolve_map_path call in apply_filter_to_surface (a Displace smart
filter does not read mapPath on re-render; upstream added that in 2cb396d1)
and no layer.smartFilter.transfer command (added in 05e98e7a), so those
hunks and the transfer test are dropped, and the trusted-edit test covers
LUTs only. The upstream mask helper keeps this base's local mask_mix.
